  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1... \nHigh pressure will maintain influence over the region through\nearly next week, resulting in prolonged dry weather and slightly\nbelow normal temperatures through Tuesday. Tonight will be the\nchilliest night of the week with widespread lows in the low to\nmid 40s expected at inland locations. A few spots across\ninterior NW PA, particularly in valleys, will likely dip into\nthe upper 30s and there is a chance that a few spots across\ninterior NE OH drop below 40 degrees early Friday morning. As\nfar as frost potential goes, 925mb flow may be a bit too high to\nallow for frost development. However, if flow lightens enough,\nthere will definitely be sufficient clearing for very isolated \ninstances of frost, particularly across far eastern \nErie/Crawford counties in PA and perhaps typical cold spots \nacross interior NE OH.\n\nHigh temperatures will generally be in the 60s through Monday or\nTuesday, although temps across the western half of the area will\nlikely warm into the lower 70s Saturday through Monday.\nWidespread low 70s are expected by the middle of next week.\n\nThe next chance of rain will arrive Wednesday through Thursday\nas a low pressure system moves across the Great Lakes region.",
